WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.859
A hugely controversial decision has been made
by YouTube, owned by Google, of course, that

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:11.230
they will be straight up removing any videos
which claim that Donald Trump lost the election

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.349
because of so-called voter fraud, which doesn't
exist.

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:16.880
Utah, YouTube, not Utah.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.900
YouTube is essentially saying Joe Biden won
the twenty twenty election.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.940
That's a historical fact at this point.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:31.170
And claims to the contrary will fall under
the umbrella of misleading videos which are

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.790
and can be restricted on YouTube.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:39.480
YouTube explains now that enough states have
certified their elections such that in total,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.610
Joe Biden has two hundred and seventy electoral
votes.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:48.600
They will remove content that, quote, misleads
people by alleging that widespread fraud or

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.340
errors change the outcome of the twenty twenty
presidential election.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.329
Now, they're not going to go and do this retroactively.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:00.620
So if you uploaded videos before yesterday
saying Trump won because of voter fraud, those

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.460
will be allowed to stay up.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.750
This is a decision that will go forward from
yesterday.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.009
YouTube explaining the decision in a series
of tweets.

00:01:08.009 --> 00:01:12.799
Let's take a look at YouTube saying our goal
this election was to connect people to authoritative

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:17.420
info, limit harmful misinformation and remove
violative content.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.780
Subsequently, authoritative news was widely
watched and recommended.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.090
And since September, we removed more than
eight thousand channels for violating our

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.549
policies.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.000
Yesterday was the safe harbor deadline.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.950
Now that enough states certify their presidential
election results will remove any content published

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.810
today or any time after.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.350
That alleges widespread fraud or errors changed
the twenty twenty US presidential outcome.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.630
Now, that's there's a couple of interesting
things there.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:45.920
Number one, it sounds like they're saying
if you are reporting about an individual instance

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.770
of of a clerical error or fraud or.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.680
Or whatever that will be allowed.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:57.060
But big picture saying Trump really won, but
because of voter fraud, Biden got it.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.859
That's what wouldn't be allowed.

00:01:58.859 --> 00:02:03.909
And the justification they're giving is that
Joe Biden's win is now simple, empirical,

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:05.639
undeniable fact.

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:06.999
YouTube going on to explain quote.

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:11.760
We'll also update today our election results
info panel, which already surfaced under two

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.680
hundred thousand vids and was shown more than
4.5 billion times.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.380
It'll note the US presidential results are
certified and linked to the twenty 20 Electoral

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.730
College results page by the Office of the
Federal Register.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.640
Lastly, saying there's always more to do.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.790
Striking the balance between openness and
responsibility is one of our toughest challenges.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.000
We're continuing to make improvements and
will apply our learnings from this election

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.280
globally.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.640
I'm actually unsure about the long term effect
of this policy and I'll explain in the sense

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.659
that I think YouTube might make life difficult
for themselves with this decision.

00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:52.299
So I am 100 percent in agreement that this
is completely within YouTube's rights as a

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:53.299
business.

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:55.470
I'm taking no issue with that whatsoever.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.410
YouTube is doing nothing illegal here, period.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:03.780
I think the implementation of this is complex
because of the doors that it opens fact checking

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.860
boxes for election content with the results
that say Joe Biden won and it's been certified

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:09.860
by states.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:15.349
I'm with it 100 percent, even demonetization
of misleading videos, which are effectively

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:16.670
conspiracy theories.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:23.400
I would even be OK with that flagging content
like Twitter does as disinformation or disputed.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.430
Often when Trump tweets, I won, absolutely
fine.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:32.780
But the complexity is they allow flat earth
content.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:37.700
They allow all sorts of other conspiracy content
that is factually wrong, so now they have

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:44.580
to make a distinction about what is factually
wrong and justifies removal.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.719
And here they're saying broad claims about
election fraud leading to Joe Biden falsely

00:03:49.719 --> 00:03:50.719
winning.

00:03:50.719 --> 00:03:54.829
That has passed a threshold where it's not
a flag, it's not sorry I hit my mic.

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:56.129
I'm getting so excited.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:03:57.170
It's not just a flag.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.350
It's not just demonetization.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.350
It's removal.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:06.500
Now, to be completely clear, the Trump actually
won stuff is completely corrosive to democracy.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.450
I've been clear and consistent on this.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.349
I'm just wondering about the enforcement of
this.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:16.609
I might even like where this goes in the sense
that it might push some of the loony right

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:20.980
wing voices to abandon YouTube altogether
and go start their own thing.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:21.980
That's great.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.940
Stop the spread of disinformation.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:29.460
But I do think YouTube is opening themselves
up to an absolute storm of insanity as a result.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.650
This is not a censorship issue to me.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.590
Biden one period YouTube can do this legally.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.560
One hundred and ten percent.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.590
But I think the enforcement is going to be
problematic.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.180
And the other thing that I find interesting
is the right wingers are going nuts about

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.370
this.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.470
And clearly, YouTube made the calculation.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.270
I mean, YouTube knew that this was going to
be an ice storm.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:56.950
When they do it, they calculated stopping
the election conspiracy theories is worth

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:03.200
it to them in exchange for the criticism that
is raining down upon them from the right for

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.200
this decision.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.930
So my concern is more about implementation
and the precedent that it sets, but we will

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.980
see ultimately how this turns out.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.690
I would love to hear your thoughts about this
decision by YouTube.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:06:26.060
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman,

